  "description": "SUKXOM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C130 H138 Gd4 Mn4 N8 O38 2+,2(H1 O1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1F (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2F (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1F (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2F (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.538-3.929 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.72-111.40°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [MnIII4GdIII4(OH)4(5)4(NO3)2(dmf)6(H2O)6](OH)2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Gd(III).",
